The '''2026–27 Ligue 1''', also known as '''Ligue 1 [[McDonald's France|McDonald's]]''' for sponsorship reasons, is the 89th season of the [[Ligue 1]], France's premier football competition.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/5359153/2024/03/21/mcdonalds-ligue-1-sponsor/|title=French football league to be rebranded as Ligue 1 McDonald's from next season|work=The New York Times |access-date=12 May 2025 |last1=Rutzler |first1=Peter |date=21 March 2024 }}</ref> It began on 21 August 2026 and is set to conclude on 29 May 2027.

[[Paris Saint-Germain FC|Paris Saint-Germain]] are the five-time defending champions.

== Teams ==
A total of eighteen teams are participating in the 2026–27 edition of the Ligue 1. [[ES Troyes AC|Troyes]] and [[Le Mans FC|Le Mans]] return to top flight after three and sixteen respective years of absence. [[FC Metz|Metz]] and [[FC Nantes|Nantes]] were relegated to [[Ligue 2]] after one and thirteen years in top flight.

